<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soleb</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Soleb is a site on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, between the Second and Third Cataracts, with a great temple built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amenhotep-iii">Amenhotep III</a> in the 14th century BCE. Dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a> and to the king himself as a god, it is the largest Egyptian temple known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, and its column bases carry lists of foreign peoples conquered or claimed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soleb.jpg" alt="Soleb" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clemens Schmillen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soleb1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
